# Fugue in C major, BWV 952 (J. S. Bach)
# A small early three-voice fugue, 4/4, 34 bars. Bar numbers match the
# Mutopia score and the MIDI (no pickup: the subject starts after a
# sixteenth rest).
#
# Character: cheerful and plain, a study piece. The subject is a run of
# sixteenths (G A B C, then turning figures down to C) and the texture is
# busy and motoric throughout, with a short minor-key middle. It wants a
# steady, easy pulse, not speed.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 72, just under two minutes. 34 bars of 4/4 is 136
# quarters. Timings found are few and disagree: a Japanese piano
# encyclopedia (enc.piano.or.jp) lists 2:00 (quarter 68); two album
# listings on ototoy.jp give 1:16 (quarter 107) and 2:11 (quarter 62),
# performers not confirmed. Pierre Hantai has recorded it (2016) but I
# found no timing. 72 is my judgment: near the 2:00 figure, a natural
# walking pace for the sixteenths.
#
# Structure (from the Mutopia LilyPond voices; I found no published
# analysis with bar numbers, so this is my own reading):
#   1-2    subject in the alto (mid), C major
#   2.5-3  answer in the soprano (top), G major
#   4-5    subject in the bass (bottom), C
#   5-7    episode modulating to G; cadence in G at bar 8
#   8-9    head in the bass (8), then the full subject in the alto in G
#          (from 8.5); the soprano rests, so the alto is the top line
#   10-11  sequence on the subject's tail, back to C
#   11.5-12 subject in the soprano, C
#   13-15  episode with suspensions over a held A in the bass (13-14),
#          D minor; half cadence on E at bar 16
#   16.5-17 subject in the bass, A minor
#   17-19  rising sequence: long notes climbing in the soprano (A, C, E,
#          G), eighths in the alto, the subject's tail in the bass
#   20-21  subject in the alto, E minor, over an E pedal in the bass
#          (20-22); cadence in E minor at bar 23
#   23.5-26 falling sequence (D minor, C, F); cadence in F at bar 26
#   27     the tail in the soprano, F
#   28     subject in the alto, C (low, on the bass staff)
#   29.5-30 subject in the bass, C: the last entry
#   31-34  coda: falling sequence with suspensions in the soprano, final
#          cadence in C

tempo 72

dyn 1 mf               # bars 1-12: exposition and the entries in G and C
lead 2.5-3 top         # bars 2.5-3: answer in the soprano
lead 4-5 bottom        # bars 4-5: subject in the bass
lead 8.5-9 top         # bars 8.5-9: alto in G, the soprano is resting so it is the top line
lead 11.5-12 top       # bars 11.5-12: subject in the soprano

dyn 13 mp              # bars 13-16: the minor-key episode, suspensions over the A
lead 16.5-17 bottom    # bars 16.5-17: subject in the bass, A minor
dyn 17 mf              # bars 17-23: the rising sequence and the E minor entry
lead 20-21 mid         # bars 20-21: subject in the alto, E minor

broaden 23 0.95        # bar 23: the E minor cadence, the main one in the middle
dyn 24 mp              # bars 24-26: the falling sequence, as an echo

dyn 27 f               # bars 27-34: back to C, the last two entries and the coda
lead 28 mid            # bar 28: subject in the alto (voices cross in 29, so stop here)
lead 29.5-30 bottom    # bars 29.5-30: subject in the bass

rit 2 0.75             # last 2 bars into the final C
